§9.1/D-10 rule 2 (S2-5.2): one decorator, one owner. The claim order is
section → table → list → blockquote → paragraph, and the owner is decided by
**what the block is**, never by which plugin happens to read the stream first:

@@{.lead, `slug-section`}
## A decorated heading

The decorator above the heading decorates the **section**, not the heading
(§9.5): the heading carries its own extras on the `#` run, so a second head
above it would be redundant.

@@unorderedA{.card, #list-1}
- one
- two

@@aside{.note}
> a decorated quote

@@{.lead, #p1}
A decorated paragraph.

A table is claimed by `table`, not by `markdown` — even though `table` runs first
and the block below is still a `Paragraph` when it reads the stream:

@@tableA{.grid, #sales}
| Produk | Harga |
| ------ | ----: |
| Laptop | 10000 |
